== Reference data & fixtures ==

Portions of the test fixture data (real EverQuest log lines and their expected
parse results, under tests/EQDeeps.Core.Tests/Fixtures/) are derived from the
parser unit tests of EQLogParser (https://github.com/kauffman12/EQLogParser),
Copyright kauffman12, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The lines
were extracted and rewritten into this project's JSON fixture format, each
paired with the parse result EQDeeps expects; the surrounding test code was not
used. Log lines themselves are EverQuest game output.

No source code from EQLogParser has been ported; EQDeeps is a clean-room
implementation. Behavior fidelity comes from documented grammars and the
fixture corpus above.

== Game-derived data ==

Two files carry data that originated with the game rather than with this
project, and EQDeeps' MIT grant does not extend to them:

- src/EQDeeps.Core/Maps/zones.tsv pairs each zone's short name with its display
  name, era and client zone ids. The ids and display names are read out of an
  EverQuest client's ZoneNames.txt (see scripts/derive-zone-eras.mjs); the eras
  and the curation are this project's own work.
- The bundled demo log (src/EQDeeps.Server/Assets/sample-log.txt.gz) is two
  days of the owner's own gameplay, cut down to the system lines the parser
  recognizes — every chat channel removed — and the monitored character renamed
  to "Sample". The other characters in those fights are named as the game named
  them.

Both are facts about the game rather than game assets, and neither contains
art, audio, or client code. They are included so the app is useful without a
game install; if Daybreak Game Company would prefer otherwise, remove them.

